Changes made to the original work
---------------------------------
As required by section 3(a)(1)(B) of CC BY 4.0, the following modifications
were made:

1. Content was SELECTED. The source guide has roughly fifty pages; this
   adaptation covers a subset, prioritizing voice and tone, language and
   grammar, punctuation, formatting, procedures, linking, code conventions,
   and the word list.

2. Content was REORGANIZED. The source is arranged as an alphabetical and
   topical reference for human lookup. This adaptation is arranged for machine
   consumption under progressive disclosure: a summary entry point (SKILL.md)
   with topic-scoped reference files loaded on demand.

3. Content was REWRITTEN. Guidance is paraphrased and condensed rather than
   reproduced. Wording, examples, and explanations differ from the original.

4. Content was ADDED. The following are original to this repository and are
   NOT part of Google developer documentation style:
   - The document-type selection table (quickstart / how-to / reference /
     concept / runbook) in SKILL.md
   - The "ten rules that matter most" ordering and framing
   - The eight-pass review checklist and its severity grading
     (Blocking / Should fix / Style / Optional)
   - All worked examples in examples/
   - All rationale text explaining why a rule exists

5. Content was OMITTED. Google-product-specific guidance (Google Cloud,
   Android, Google Workspace annotations and product naming rules) is largely
   omitted as inapplicable outside Google documentation, except where it
   illustrates a general principle.

